e start of her maiden voyage in 1628 must be one of the strangest tales of the sea.","start":23.38,"end":30.27,"score":0.994,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-003","sourceId":"b4-027-003","sourceIndex":2,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,20],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"For nearly three and a half centuries she lay at the bottom of Stockholm harbour until her discovery in 1956.","start":31.3,"end":39.29,"score":0.958,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-004","sourceId":"b4-027-004","sourceIndex":3,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,11],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"This was the Vasa, royal flagship of the great imperial fleet.","start":40.18,"end":45.44,"score":0.975,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-005-p01","sourceId":"b4-027-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,19],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"King Gustavus Adolphus 'The Northern Hurricane', then at the height of his military success in the 'Thirty Years' War,","start":46.88,"end":54.65,"score":0.927,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-005-p02","sourceId":"b4-027-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[19,25],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"had dictated her measurements and armament.","start":55.43,"end":58.28,"score":0.924,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-006","sourceId":"b4-027-006","sourceIndex":5,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,6],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"Triple gun-decks mounted sixty-four bronze cannon.","start":59.38,"end":62.72,"score":0.945,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-007","sourceId":"b4-027-007","sourceIndex":6,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"She was intended to play a leading role in the growing might of Sweden.","start":63.55,"end":67.81,"score":0.985,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-008","sourceId":"b4-027-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"As she was prepared for her maiden voyage on August 10, 1628, Stockholm was in a ferment.","start":69.15,"end":76.7,"score":0.968,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-009","sourceId":"b4-027-009","sourceIndex":8,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,22],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"From the Skeppsbron and surrounding islands the people watched this thing of beauty begin to spread her sails and catch the wind.","start":77.52,"end":86.04,"score":0.961,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-010-p01","sourceId":"b4-027-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,13],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"They had laboured for three years to produce this floating work of art;","start":87.03,"end":90.96,"score":0.978,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-010-p02","sourceId":"b4-027-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[13,24],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"she was more richly carved and ornamented than any previous ship.","start":91.94,"end":96.08,"score":0.983,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-011-p01","sourceId":"b4-027-011","sourceIndex":10,"part":1,"parts":3,"wordRange":[0,16],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The high stern castle was a riot of carved gods, demons, knights, kings, warriors, mermaids, cherubs;","start":97.18,"end":106.78,"score":0.896,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-011-p02","sourceId":"b4-027-011","sourceIndex":10,"part":2,"parts":3,"wordRange":[16,31],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"and zoomorphic animal shapes ablaze with red and gold and blue, symbols of courage, power,","start":107.04,"end":114.99,"score":0.951,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-011-p03","sourceId":"b4-027-011","sourceIndex":10,"part":3,"parts":3,"wordRange":[31,46],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"and cruelty, were portrayed to stir the imaginations of the superstitious sailors of the day.","start":115.42,"end":122.16,"score":0.896,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-012","sourceId":"b4-027-012","sourceIndex":11,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Then the cannons of the anchored warships thundered a salute to which the Vasa fired in reply.","start":123.603,"end":130.32,"score":0.928,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-013-p01","sourceId":"b4-027-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":1,"parts":4,"wordRange":[0,19],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"As she emerged from her drifting cloud of gun smoke with the water churned to foam beneath her bow,","start":131.5,"end":137.7,"score":0.951,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-013-p02","sourceId":"b4-027-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":2,"parts":4,"wordRange":[19,24],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"her flags flying, pennants waving,","start":138.44,"end":141.44,"score":0.948,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-013-p03","sourceId":"b4-027-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":3,"parts":4,"wordRange":[24,40],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"sails filling in the breeze, and the red and gold or her superstructure ablaze with colour,","start":142.05,"end":147.91,"score":0.865,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":true,"reviewReasons":["low-word-confidence"]},{"id":"b4-027-013-p04","sourceId":"b4-027-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":4,"parts":4,"wordRange":[40,52],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"she presented a more majestic spectacle than Stockholmers had ever seen before.","start":148.65,"end":154.09,"score":0.989,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-014","sourceId":"b4-027-014","sourceIndex":13,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,11],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"All gun-ports were open and the muzzles peeped wickedly from them.","start":155.34,"end":159.82,"score":0.954,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-015","sourceId":"b4-027-015","sourceIndex":14,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,19],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"As the wind freshened there came a sudden squall and the ship made a strange movement, listing to port.","start":161.04,"end":168.32,"score":0.957,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-016-p01","sourceId":"b4-027-016","sourceIndex":15,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,17],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The Ordnance officer ordered all the port cannon to be heaved to starboard to counteract the list","start":169.283,"end":175.24,"score":0.926,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-016-p02","sourceId":"b4-027-016","sourceIndex":15,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[17,25],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"but the steepening angle of the decks increased.","start":175.723,"end":178.72,"score":0.981,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-017-p01","sourceId":"b4-027-017","sourceIndex":16,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,15],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Then the sound of rumbling thunder reached the watchers on the shore, as cargo, ballast,","start":179.72,"end":186.21,"score":0.918,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-017-p02","sourceId":"b4-027-017","sourceIndex":16,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[15,33],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"ammunition and 400 people went sliding and crashing down to the port side of the steeply listing ship.","start":186.64,"end":193.84,"score":0.958,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-018","sourceId":"b4-027-018","sourceIndex":17,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The lower gun-ports were now below water and the inrush sealed the ship's fate.","start":194.822,"end":200.84,"score":0.957,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-019-p01","sourceId":"b4-027-019","sourceIndex":18,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,15],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"In that first glorious hour, the mighty Vasa, which was intended to rule the Baltic,","start":201.88,"end":207.9,"score":0.966,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b4-027-019-p02","sourceId":"b4-027-019","sourceIndex":18,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[15,25],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"sank with all flags flying--in the harbour of her birth.","start":208.35,"end":212.64,"score":0.942,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]}]}
